    <string name="browse_repo_size">"  ·  Size "</string>
    <string name="browse_repo_note1">\n\nThis \"repo\" is the full git history, including all commits, all branches, and the .git directory.</string>
    <string name="browse_repo_note2">What actually downloads is a zip snapshot of the latest default branch, usually much smaller —</string>
    <string name="browse_repo_note3">So even a repo of several hundred MB can finish downloading in seconds.</string>
    <string name="browse_gh_note1">\n\nNot every GitHub repo can be installed directly: it downloads a zip of the default branch,</string>
    <string name="browse_gh_note2">It strips the outermost folder and puts it in Mods/. Repos without any .lua files are rejected.</string>
