    <string name="help_title">Folder conventions\n</string>
    <string name="help_path">Documents/Balatro/game/save/Mods/&lt;mod name&gt;/\n</string>
    <string name="help_one_level">A mod must have exactly one folder level — don\'t nest it deeper.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_nested_q">What does \"nested an extra level\" mean?\n</string>
    <string name="help_nested_a">Many unzip tools create an extra folder named after the zip file, and then the game won\'t recognize the mod at all.</string>
    <string name="help_nested_fix">If you see this mark, delete it and reinstall with \"Install ZIP\" — the installer strips the extra level automatically.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_no_perm">No permissions needed\n</string>
    <string name="help_saf">It uses the system Storage Access Framework and can only read and write the folder you picked when selecting the directory.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_online">Installing mods online\n</string>
    <string name="help_online_a">The \"Hot\" tab at the bottom opens the online catalog, with two sources to switch between:</string>
    <string name="help_online_b">Thunderstore sorts by downloads, GitHub by stars. Opening a detail page shows the description (translated into your system language when needed),</string>
    <string name="help_online_c">then tap \"Download &amp; install\" to install it. Already-installed packages are marked with a green OK.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_gh_a">Not every GitHub repo can be installed: the manager downloads a zip of the default branch,</string>
    <string name="help_gh_b">It strips the outermost folder and puts it in Mods; repos without any .lua files are rejected.</string>
    <string name="help_lang_hint">The language tag in the list is a useful hint — Lua repos are the ones most likely to work.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_limits">Known limitations\n</string>
    <string name="help_lovely_ver">"Built-in Lovely is 0.9.0. Some mods write patches in 0.10 syntax, so the log may show "</string>
    <string name="help_native">warnings like \"Unknown key\"; mods with native components (e.g. Talisman) can\'t run on phones.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_log_title">Logs are cleaned up automatically\n</string>
    <string name="help_log_a">The game writes a lovely-*.log on every launch, which piles up over time.</string>
    <string name="help_log_b">The manager automatically deletes logs older than 1 hour when you refresh or view logs,</string>
    <string name="help_log_c">and always keeps the newest one, so the log view is never empty.\n\n</string>
    <string name="help_bg_title">Background\n</string>
    <string name="help_bg_a">Ported from the game\'s original background.fs shader (polar swirl + three-color blend).</string>
    <string name="help_bg_b">"The original palette is red, black and white; this uses the teal palette from Cryptid\'s rework — "</string>
    <string name="help_bg_c">That color was swapped in by Cryptid — it\'s not the original.</string>
